						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#486">Mage Focus items</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Hey all, just a little information I have suspected and finally proved to myself by actually working out the math. Mages in a recent patch (6 months ago or so) were given some new summonable items that Increased duration of buffs, reduced aggro, reduced mana used on casting and increased damage done with DD's. All the above were claimed to be 10%. Now when u cast a spell costing 250 mana, 25 mana off that is significant and add 10% damage to a DD it effectively gives you 20% or more in combination for mana spent. Well here is the great news, Seems the Bracer is actually adding 15% more damage to DD's or more. When I use a shock spell and it kicks the damage from 176 to 211, that's a bit more than 10%, it works out to be 16.58% increase in damage for a mana cost of 90% of the original. Now at lvl 44 I get a DD spell doing 580 points for 250 mana, or, 580 points for 225 mana using the ring. Now add the Bracer and so mar my max damage has been 690 damage for 225 mana. That is an increase of 15.94% damage using 10% less mana. What this means collectively is you are getting roughly 25% more for you mana used if using the two focus items that affect mana and damage than you did before. Try them out and see if you are a Damage caster. This also affects the buffs you use on yourself and others too. Basically an increase of 20% efficiency over not using them. Just letting you all know if you have an important or dangerous camp, go try to get the items or come to me for them. I can supply the items needed for up to lvl 44 for buffs, mana used and aggro, and up to lvl 54 for damage increase.
						</td>
					</tr>
